    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111-a1">

                <pb facs="0175" n="99" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg99"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the Acting Minister for Foreign
                        Affairs </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 460</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 9, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your excellency’s note of June 6, 1916, informing me of the sad death
                    of His Excellency Yuan Shih-kai, President of the Republic of China, at 10 a.m.,
                    on June 6.</p>
                <pb facs="0176" n="100" xml:id="pg100"/>
                <p>Upon receipt of your excellency’s note I sent a telegram to my Government, and
                    have now received an instruction directing me to convey to your excellency’s
                    Government the deep regret and sincere sympathy of the Government of the United
                    States and of the Secretary of State.</p>
                <p>I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paul S. Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
